# Engineering lifecycle gates

When a request involves **implementing a non-trivial feature**, first check whether the required upstream documentation exists and is **`Approved`** (per the gate list below). If not, **stop** and enter planning/design mode — invoke the relevant skill(s) to produce or update the missing documentation — rather than modifying application source code directly.

**Exempt:** trivial fixes (typos, formatting, obvious bugs with no behavior/design change).

## Permanent gates

A gate is satisfied only when its required documents are `Approved`, not merely `Draft`.

| Gate | Phase | Required artifacts |
|---|---|---|
| 0 | Project initiation | Project Charter |
| 1 | Product definition | PRD |
| 2 | Requirements | SRS, traceability |
| 3 | Architecture | Architecture docs, ADRs (as needed) |
| 4 | Detailed design | Relevant database / API / ML / error-handling design |
| 5 | Implementation planning | Implementation Plan |
| 6 | Implementation | Code (with `# Implements: FR-XXX` on modules listed in the plan) |
| 7 | Verification | Tests, CI, quality checks; test strategy/plan docs live here |
| 8 | Release | Deployment notes, release notes as applicable |
| 9 | Operations | Monitoring/incident/change process as applicable |

Change Requests re-enter at **Gate 2 (Requirements)**.

Gates govern when a **phase** may start. Per-task **Definition of Done** lives in the Implementation Plan and governs when a single `IMP-XXX` is finished.

**§22 / Gate 6 precondition:** Before non-trivial **Gate 6** coding, require **Approved** Implementation Plan **and** **Approved** Test Strategy (prefer Test Plan too). Gate 7’s *number* (verification after implementation) refers to executing and closing verification — it does **not** allow Test Strategy to stay Draft while coding starts. See `docs/00-meta/gates.md`.

## Skills to invoke (not optional brainstorming)

| Need | Skill |
|---|---|
| Charter / PRD | `project-discovery` |
| SRS / traceability | `requirements` |
| System/data/API/ML/infra architecture | `architecture` |
| ADRs only | `architecture-decisions` |
| IMP plan / annotation targets | `implementation-planning` |
| Test strategy/plan | `testing` |
| CI/CD, infra, deploy, ops | `devops-operations` |
| Audits / drift | `engineering-review` |

## Grill-Me

For decisions only the user can make, invoke **Grill-Me** (`.cursor/skills/grill-me/`) before `[OPEN QUESTION]` / invented assumptions. `engineering-review` does **not** call Grill-Me.

## Source-of-truth reminders

- Charter ≠ PRD (no duplication)
- Design vs contract vs implementation disagreement is a **defect**
- ADR files only via `architecture-decisions`
- Do not invent product facts, metrics, or users

## Docs root

Living docs live under `docs/`. See `docs/00-meta/documentation-guide.md`.
